      "description": "Watch Lens vs Auxerre highlights and goals from Ligue 1 on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 22, 2026. The stage was set for a high-stakes Ligue 1 encounter as two sides with contrasting ambitions clashed under the lights. Fans expected a tactical battle, and they were treated to an afternoon of relentless drama on 2026-08-22 . Early Drama and Red Card Chaos The match ignited in the 11th minute when Arthur Piedfort was penalized for a handball inside the box. After a tense VAR review, the referee pointed to the spot, allowing Florian Thauvin to calmly slot the ball home with his left foot. Lens took an early lead, and their advantage grew even more significant when Auxerre were reduced to ten men. Christ Makosso received a straight red card in the 35th minute for a professional foul as the last man, a decision that sparked protests and even saw Lens manager Will Still receive a yellow card for his reaction on the touchline. Second Half Goal Frenzy Following the interval, Lens clinical efficiency came to the fore. Franjo Ivanovic doubled the lead in the 49th minute after being set up by Abdallah Sima , and Saud Abdulhamid added a third with a powerful header shortly after. While Auxerre managed to pull one back through a Danny Namaso penalty in the 61st minute, the momentum remained firmly with the hosts. Pierre Ganiou made it 4-1 following a smart assist from Michal Skoras , effectively ending the contest as a spectacle of competition. In a chaotic final ten minutes, Auxerre found a second goal through Lamine Sy , but the spotlight returned to Florian Thauvin . In the 88th minute, a penalty for Lens was initially missed by Thauvin , but a VAR intervention ordered a retake due to an infringement. He made no mistake on his second attempt, firing into the corner to secure a 5-2 victory. Lens saw out the final moments with 53% possession, celebrating a well-deserved win after a display of attacking prowess."
